INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('0a3239d4-b0ce-5ef5-ac78-3b1b7c751af5', 'USA Disclosure of Payments by Resource Extraction Issuers', 'Disclosure of Payments by Resource Extraction Issuers', 'This SEC rule, issued under Section 1504 of the Dodd-Frank Act, mandates that U.S.-listed resource extraction companies (oil, gas, and mining firms) disclose payments made to foreign governments and the U.S. federal government. The rule aims to increase transparency, reduce corruption risks, and promote accountability in the extractive industries.

Key provisions include:

Scope & Applicability:
Applies to publicly traded companies (issuers) engaged in resource extraction.
Covers entities that develop oil, natural gas, or minerals.
Mandatory Payment Disclosures:
Companies must report all payments related to resource extraction, including:
Taxes, royalties, fees, production entitlements, bonuses, and infrastructure payments.
Payments exceeding $100,000 per fiscal year.
Reports must identify the government receiving the payment, project details, and the payment type.
Annual Reporting Requirements:
Filings must be made using Form SD under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934.
Companies must publicly disclose payment data in annual reports.
Alignment with International Transparency Standards:
The rule aligns with global anti-corruption efforts, including the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI).
This rule enhances corporate transparency, promotes ethical governance, and strengthens investor confidence in resource extraction industries.', 'This SEC rule, issued under Section 1504 of the Dodd-Frank Act, mandates that U.S.-listed resource extraction companies (oil, gas, and mining firms) disclose payments made to foreign governments and the U.S. federal government. The rule aims to increase transparency, reduce corruption risks, and promote accountability in the extractive industries.

