Public Disclosure & Transparency:
The EPA publishes emissions data for public access, enhancing corporate accountability.
Enforcement & Penalties:
Facilities failing to comply face administrative penalties and enforcement actions under the Clean Air Act (CAA) Section 114.
GHGRP provides crucial emissions data that supports state and federal climate policies, corporate sustainability strategies, and international reporting frameworks.', 'The Mandatory Greenhouse Gas Reporting Program (GHGRP) was established by the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) under 40 CFR Part 98, requiring certain facilities and suppliers to report their greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions. The regulation aims to improve data transparency, inform climate policies, and enhance emissions tracking.

